  <name>Omnilogue</name>
  <summary>Browse and search the history of your AI coding assistants</summary>
  <developer id="io.github.jhlee0409">
    <name>JaeHyeok Lee</name>
  </developer>

  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>MIT</project_license>

  <description>
    <p>
      Omnilogue (formerly Claude Code History Viewer) reads the conversation history that AI
      coding assistants keep on your computer and lets you browse, search and analyze it in one
      place. Everything stays on your machine.
    </p>
    <p>It reads the local history of:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Claude Code, Codex CLI, Gemini CLI and Antigravity</li>
      <li>Cursor, Cline, GitHub Copilot and VS Code chat</li>
      <li>Aider, OpenCode, ForgeCode, CodeBuddy Code, Grok CLI and more</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Features:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Full-text search across every session and provider</li>
      <li>Token usage, cost and activity statistics per session, project and day</li>
      <li>Recent file edits made by the assistants, with their diffs</li>
      <li>Session renaming, archiving and export</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The assistants keep their history in your home folder and every session points at the
      project folder it ran in, so this app can read your home folder. It can only write to the
      assistants' own history folders (to rename or delete sessions), to its own settings, and to
      your Downloads folder for exports.
    </p>
  </description>

